{"source":"PAGEEDITOR","folderId":null,"values":{"sites":[{"id":"7483257320154fb9b1e3d5ee14209e9d","title":"Marine Cadastre Hub"}],"layout":{"sections":[{"containment":"fixed","isFooter":false,"style":{"background":{"isFile":false,"isUrl":true,"state":"","display":{},"transparency":0,"position":{"x":"center","y":"center"},"color":"transparent"},"color":"#312a35","rowLayout":"box"},"rows":[{"cards":[{"component":{"name":"markdown-card","settings":{"cardId":"ckptx1xop","schemaVersion":2.1,"markdown":"<p class=\"section-header\">Disclaimer</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This agreement sets forth the terms and conditions that apply to your access and use of Marine Cadastre. In addition, when using particular services on Marine Cadastre, you shall be subject to any guidelines for such services that may be posted and revised by data providers from time to time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>By accessing or using Marine Cadastre, you agree to accept these terms and conditions of use. Marine Cadastre reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to amend or modify these terms and conditions of use, or may impose new conditions at any time. Any such changes will be reflected by an updated version of this posting (dated 1 July 2020). Any use of the Marine Cadastre site by you after such posting shall be deemed to constitute acceptance by you of such changes, modifications, or additions. If, at any time, you do not wish to accept this agreement, you may choose not to access and use Marine Cadastre.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"section-header\">Terms and Conditions</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The information on this website is intended for general informational purposes only and is not to be construed as legal advice. For legal compliance purposes, please consult the appropriate statutes and regulations. The application and effect of laws can vary widely according to the specific facts involved. For interpretation of the appropriate statutes and regulations for your individual needs, please consult a competent attorney.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In preparation of this site, every effort has been made to offer the most up-to-date and accurate information possible. The Marine Cadastre team works closely with data providers and stakeholders to identify which data are appropriate to serve or reference on the site, and to ensure their suitability for marine planning. The Marine Cadastre team follows the NOAA guidelines for pre-dissemination review by assessing the quality, integrity, and objectivity of data available through the site and employs detailed standard operating procedures as part of its normal activities. More detailed information on Marine Cadastre quality assurance processes is available upon request.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Nevertheless, inadvertent errors in information may occur. In particular, Marine Cadastre disclaims any responsibility for typographical errors and accuracy of the information that may be contained on the Marine Cadastre website. The information included on the Marine Cadastre website has been compiled from a variety of sources and is subject to change without notice to the user. Marine Cadastre makes no warranties or representations whatsoever regarding the availability, quality, accuracy, content, completeness, or suitability for the user’s needs of such information. The services, information, and data made available on the Marine Cadastre website are provided “as is” without warranties of any kind.\r\n\r\n<p>There are links and pointers to external Internet websites contained in the Marine Cadastre website, provided for the convenience of the user. The appearance of external links on this World Wide Web site does not constitute endorsement by Marine Cadastre of external websites or the information, products, or services contained therein. For other than authorized activities, Marine Cadastre does not exercise any editorial control over the information the user may find at these locations. These links are provided consistent with the stated purpose of the Marine Cadastre website. Marine Cadastre does not assume any responsibility or liability for any information available at such linked sites, or at any link contained in a linked site. Any references in the Marine Cadastre to any organizations, products, or services do not necessarily constitute or imply endorsement or recommendation of those organizations, products, or services by Marine Cadastre.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>By using the Marine Cadastre, the user assumes the risks associated with the use of this site, including any risk to the user’s computer, software, or data being damaged by any virus, software, or any other file which might be transmitted or activated while the user accesses this webpage.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The information on government servers is in the public domain, unless specifically annotated otherwise, and may be used freely by the user so long as the user does not 1) claim the information is the user’s own (e.g., by claiming copyright for an organization or the government), 2) use the information in a manner that implies an endorsement by or affiliation with the government, or 3) modify the information in content and then present it as official government material. The user also cannot present information of his or her own in a way that makes it appear to be official government information.</p>"}},"width":12}]}],"visibility":{"access":"default","groups":[]}}]},"updatedAt":"2025-11-13T16:32:38.964Z","updatedBy":"supriya.khadke_noaa"}}